From: C4risrocks <C4risrocks@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:23:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?gpu:=20the=20Metal=20spike=20(M0)=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20one=20window,=20one=20CAMetalLayer,=20a=20timed=20triangle?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

a --renderer metal backend behind the metal feature: device + queue +
a CAMetalLayer hung on the window's NSView, one oversized triangle
presented per frame through a small MSL source, drawable sizing tied
to the window's scale. the presentation-test completion line stays
backend-agnostic. this spike answers M0's numbers question: the
on-screen present loop paces at 60 fps like the Vulkan path does.
